message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "adaptFVC"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nakajima
    given-names: Kota
    affiliation: "Okayama University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-8111-9021"
abstract: >-
  adaptFVC is an application for calculating fractional vegetation cover (FVC)
  from visible-light (RGB) images of crop canopies. The user clicks plant and
  soil pixels on a few images, and adaptFVC trains a Random Forest classifier
  on the CIELAB colour of those pixels and labels every pixel of every image in
  the folder as plant or soil. A separate model is meant to be built for each
  set of images taken in the same field, on the same day, with the same camera.
version: "3.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-10"
